{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver arrived at the pickup at 12:15:30 and cancelled at 12:21:10, after the 300-second free wait required by POL-NS-21, so the no-show fee of 5.00 SGD is properly chargeable under POL-NS-22.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-GPS-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver placed two in-app calls to the rider, at 12:17:55 and 12:19:40, both before cancellation. The rider admits the calls in their own claim text. This satisfies the call requirement of POL-NS-23.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own message 'Coming down now, sorry' was sent at 12:21:50, after the free wait expired and after the driver cancelled. This confirms the rider was not at the pickup point and was a genuine no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim that no in-app chat message was sent is true, but the driver's two in-app calls, which the rider admits, constitute sufficient contact under POL-NS-23. The rider's phone was on silent, so a chat message would have been equally ineffective. The missing message is not a ground to void the fee where the driver made reasonable and repeated contact attempts.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was notified by the platform push at 12:15:34 ('Your driver has arrived'), and the driver called twice; the rider's later apology shows they were aware of the driver's presence. The fee should stand as the rider failed to board within the free wait.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.events",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim is not supported because the driver's two in-app calls, admitted by the rider, satisfied the contact obligation in substance, and the rider's own late message confirms they were a no-show. The present state should stand.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.claim_text",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the no-show fee stands, the ruling should be DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00, as the fee was properly charged and transferred to the driver under POL-NS-22.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "You were charged a 5.00 SGD no-show fee when the driver cancelled TRP-05053 at 12:21:10. The rider's dispute succeeds, and the whole 5.00 SGD is returned.\n\nThe reason is POL-NS-23, the driver's contact obligation. Before cancelling for a no-show, the driver must have BOTH sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call, each before cancellation. The record shows the calls were made — two in-app calls at 12:17:55 and 12:19:40, both unanswered, both before the 12:21:10 cancellation (EV-TRIP-05053). But the message limb fails: the chat log (EV-CHAT-05053) contains no driver message at all, and the trip record's contact check (EV-TRIP-05053) reports message_count 0 and obligation_met false. The only message on the trip is the rider's own 'Coming down now, sorry', sent at 12:21:50 — 40 seconds after the cancellation — so it cannot be a driver message sent before cancelling. POL-NS-23 is conjunctive: the missing message alone voids the fee. The driver's argument that the two calls and the push notification amounted to reasonable contact cannot override the clause's plain requirement of both a message and a call, and whether the rider's phone was on silent does not change the test.\n\nThe free wait under POL-NS-21 was in fact satisfied (arrival 12:15:30, cancellation 340 s later, past the 300 s free wait), but POL-NS-21 and POL-NS-23 are separate, cumulative conditions, and a fee the contact obligation voids cannot be resurrected by the wait. POL-NS-22's driver compensation applies only 'where the fee stands', so the driver receives nothing here.\n\nThe money figures are read from the fare ledger (EV-FARE-05053): 5.00 SGD charged, refund_issued_sgd 0.00. Under POL-GEN-03 the rider is entirely right, so this is a FULL_REFUND of 5.00 SGD, with driver_compensation_sgd null.\n\nNo referral fires. The fee charged was exactly 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not apply; the driver did attempt contact, so POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not apply; and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show counter is not present on the rider profile (and the fee does not stand in any event).\n\nThe contested value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD first band, so under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling is final.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the 5.00 SGD no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-05053 is voided and returned to you in full, so amount_sgd is 5.00 and driver_compensation_sgd is null. The governing clause is POL-NS-23 (the driver's contact obligation), which requires that, before cancelling for a no-show, the driver both sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call. The trip record EV-TRIP-05053 (contact_before_cancel) shows call_count 2 but message_count 0 with an empty messages array and sets obligation_met false; the chat log EV-CHAT-05053 carries exactly one entry, your own message at 12:21:50, which is 40 seconds after the 12:21:10 cancellation. The message limb is therefore unmet, and POL-NS-23 voids the fee with no driver compensation. The fare ledger EV-FARE-05053 confirms the sums: cancellation_fee 5.00, total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.0. The free-wait requirement in POL-NS-21 was in fact satisfied - the driver's arrival at 12:15:30 is corroborated by the GPS trace EV-GPS-05053 (nearest fix 3.07 m from the pickup at 12:16:44, accuracy 6.0 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius) and the 12:21:10 cancellation came 340 s later, past the 300 s free wait - but POL-NS-21 and POL-NS-23 are separate and cumulative requirements, and the fee does not survive the contact obligation. To the driver: your two in-app calls at 12:17:55 and 12:19:40 are on the record and the rider does not deny them, but POL-NS-23 is conjunctive - a message is required as well as a call - so two unanswered calls cannot carry the fee, and the rider's phone being on silent does not change the clause's test. Your counterparty statement ('I called two times, no answer') asserts calls only and says nothing about any message, which is consistent with the zero-message record. No referral is produced: the fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD in POL-NS-22, the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter for POL-NS-25, and POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not fire because the driver did arrive and did attempt contact. Confidence 0.95; the deciding facts rest on EV-TRIP-05053 and EV-CHAT-05053, both weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
